    <node id="P031-C0031"><data key="label">Qualified ``theory birth&#x27;&#x27;: The induced endomap E_ tau,f packages a distribution by evolving for tau steps and then forgetting micro-detail below the lens f , re-instantiating it via the chosen prototypes. Theorem shows that a small retention error implies sm…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0032"><data key="label">Define the (undirected) support graph G=(Z,E) by declaring \ i,j\ ∈ E iff P_ ij &gt;0 (equivalently P_ ji &gt;0 by A_REV). Let E be the corresponding set of oriented edges: for each \ i,j\ ∈ E we include both (i,j) and (j,i) .</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0033"><data key="label">Edge log-ratio 1-form: Assume A_FIN+A_REV. The antisymmetric edge 1-form associated to P is the function a: E→ R defined by a_ ij := a(i,j) := P_ ij P_ ji for (i,j)∈ E. Then a_ ji =-a_ ij .</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0034"><data key="label">Why A_REV matters: If A_REV fails, then ratios such as P_ ij /P_ ji may be undefined, and many time-reversal quantities become infinite rather than merely nonzero. In this paper we treat A_REV as the basic finiteness/admissibility condition for edge log-ratio…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
