    <node id="P031-C0043"><data key="label">Stationarity is not required (L-AOT-STAT-01): The quantity Sigma_T(rho) is defined for any initial distribution rho ; it can be strictly positive even in a detailed-balance chain when rho is not stationary (a boundary-term effect). Stationarity is only needed…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0044"><data key="label">Steady-state entropy production (D-AOT-EP-01): Assume additionally A_STAT and let pi be a stationary distribution for P . The (finite-horizon) steady-state entropy production is EP_T:=Sigma_T(pi) . When a per-step rate is desired, we write ep:= 1TSigma_T(pi)…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
