    <node id="P031-C0051"><data key="label">Predicates and definability: A (Boolean) predicate is a function h:Z→\ 0,1\ . We say that h is definable from the theory f (equivalently: Pi_f -measurable) if it is constant on each block: x∈ X,\ z,z&#x27;∈ B_x, h(z)=h(z&#x27;). Equivalently, there exists h:X→\ 0,1\ wi…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0052"><data key="label">In a fixed finite Z there is a hard cap on how many strict refinements are possible; open-endedness is modeled by repeated extensions across growing problems/domains (each step finite). The ``finite forcing lemma&#x27;&#x27; is a combinatorial proxy and does not claim…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0053"><data key="label">Counting lemma: definable predicates are rare: Let N:=|Z| and K:=|X| . [Counting definable predicates] Assume A_FIN+A_LENS. The number of predicates definable from f:Z→ X is exactly 2^K . Consequently, if h is sampled uniformly from \ 0,1\ ^Z , then P(h is de…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0054"><data key="label">Counting definable predicates: Assume A_FIN+A_LENS. The number of predicates definable from f:Z→ X is exactly 2^K . Consequently, if h is sampled uniformly from \ 0,1\ ^Z , then P(h is definable from f)= 2^K 2^N =2^ -(N-K) .</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0055"><data key="label">Finite forcing lemma / physical forcing lemma: Assume A_FIN+A_LENS. Let f:Z→ X be a theory with blocks Pi_f=\ B_x\ _ x∈ X , and sample h:Z→\ 0,1\ uniformly from \ 0,1\ ^Z (i.i.d.\ fair bits across microstates). Then non-definability is generic: P(h is not def…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0056"><data key="label">The ``Nothing Stays Constant&#x27;&#x27; Lemma.: Assume A_FIN+A_LENS and let f:Z→ X have blocks Pi_f=\ B_x\ _ x∈ X . For each block B_x , P(h is constant on B_x)=2^ 1-|B_x| , and by a union bound, P( x∈ X such that h is constant on B_x)\ \ _ x∈ X 2^ 1-|B_x| . In partic…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0057"><data key="label">Assume A_FIN+A_LENS and let f:Z→ X have blocks Pi_f=\ B_x\ _ x∈ X . For each block B_x , P(h is constant on B_x)=2^ 1-|B_x| , and by a union bound, P( x∈ X such that h is constant on B_x)\ \ _ x∈ X 2^ 1-|B_x| . In particular, if every block has size at least…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0058"><data key="label">Generic extension is strict: Assume A_FIN+A_LENS. With probability 1-2^ -(N-K) , the refined lens (f,h):Z→ X×\ 0,1\ is a strict refinement of f . Equivalently, it distinguishes at least one pair of microstates previously indistinguishable under f .</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0059"><data key="label">Why this is the anti-saturation move: Closure (or packaging) at a fixed theory saturates by idempotence: repeated closure steps do not create an infinite strict chain. Corollary exhibits a mathematically clean extension step: adjoining a generic predicate cha…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0060"><data key="label">Process soup (D-META-PROC-01): A process soup is a set P equipped with a partially defined associative composition (a partial semigroup), with identities where relevant.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0061"><data key="label">Interface lens (D-META-LENS-01): An interface lens is a map f: P→ X to a set of observables. It induces a kernel equivalence x _f y iff f(x)=f(y) . Limited access means x≠ y with x _f y . This abstracts the notion of a coarse-graining lens f:Z→ X used elsewhe…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0062"><data key="label">Refinement family (D-META-REF-01): A refinement family is a chain of equivalence relations ( _j)_ j 0 with x _ j+1 y implies x _j y ; equivalently, lenses f_j with f_j=g_j f_ j+1 for some maps g_j . As j increases, observables become more discriminating (part…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0063"><data key="label">Bounded interface (D-META-BND-01): There exists C_0 1 such that the quotient index satisfies | P/ _j| C_0(j+1) for all j . This is an explicit bounded-interface hypothesis on the lens hierarchy (a modeling assumption encoding bounded observable signature); it…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0064"><data key="label">Self-generated primitives: Assume D-META-PROC-01, D-META-LENS-01, D-META-REF-01, and D-META-BND-01. Then the six primitives P1–P6 appear canonically as closure mechanics. Here P5, P6, P4, and P2 are by construction from the lens/refinement data, while P1 and…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0065"><data key="label">Definitions of P1–P6: [P1: operator rewrite] P1 is a rewrite of the substrate operator: replace a Markov kernel P by a new kernel P&#x27; (or a finite family \ P^ (m) \ ), thereby changing the endomap mu↦ mu P^tau and the induced empirical endomap E_ tau,f . This…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0066"><data key="label">P1: operator rewrite: P1 is a rewrite of the substrate operator: replace a Markov kernel P by a new kernel P&#x27; (or a finite family \ P^ (m) \ ), thereby changing the endomap mu↦ mu P^tau and the induced empirical endomap E_ tau,f . This is a change in the oper…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0067"><data key="label">P2: gating / constraints: P2 restricts the support graph by deleting edges (setting selected P_ ij =0 ) and renormalizing rows, or equivalently restricting to a subgraph on which the kernel lives. Cycle-rank claims are interpreted on the undirected support gr…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0068"><data key="label">P3: autonomous protocol holonomy: P3 is modeled in the autonomous lifted form on Z:=X×Phi . The phase phi∈Phi evolves by an internal kernel S , and conditioned on phi the microstate updates by K_phi . No external schedule is assumed in the main text; external…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0069"><data key="label">P4: sectors / invariants: P4 is a conserved sector label: the support decomposes into disconnected components (block structure), or equivalently P is block diagonal up to permutation, so evolution preserves a sector coordinate.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0070"><data key="label">P5: packaging: P5 is an idempotent endomap e whose fixed points Fix(e) are the packaged objects of a given theory. This is an endomap notion (Section ). It is not an order-closure.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0071"><data key="label">P6: accounting / audit: P6 is an accounting/audit structure: a certificate or functional that is monotone under coarse maps or packaging. Canonical instantiations in this manuscript include: the information/feasibility order induced by limited access (META),…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0072"><data key="label">We write P6_drive for the ACC specialization: a non-exact log-ratio 1-form (equivalently, a nonzero cycle integral). This is the condition used in the slogan ``P3 needs P6_drive&#x27;&#x27; under autonomy.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
