    <node id="P031-C0075"><data key="label">P2 gating shrinks cycle space: T-P2-01. Assume A_FIN+A_REV. Let G=(V,E) be an undirected support graph and let G&#x27;=(V,E&#x27;) be obtained by deleting edges. Then beta_1(G&#x27;) beta_1(G), beta_1(G) :=|E|-|V|+c(G), where c(G) is the number of connected components.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P031-C0076"><data key="label">P1 can change cycle rank and spectral gap (T-P1-01): Assume A_FIN+A_REV. P1 rewrites can increase or decrease cycle rank and can increase or decrease a metastability proxy (the spectral gap of a reversible lazy random walk).</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
