    <node id="P026-C0012"><data key="label">The paper does not assert that every phenomenon, every theory, or all of mathematics reduces to six primitives. The calculus accepts a directed-cell judgment P_ i P_ j only under the per-cell admissibility predicate and per-cell profile of Subsection 4.3, and…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P026-C0013"><data key="label">The paper does not assert that the four model families — PICA, Cantor, abstract interpretation, and graph/cohomology — realize the entire calculus or supply universal theorem sources.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P026-C0014"><data key="label">The paper does not assert that any instrument certifies its own complete soundness at the same level, nor that the calculus admits a final self-certifying instrument on a finite tower.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
