    <node id="P028-C0025"><data key="label">The theorem does not re-prove the Needle Killer or Navier–Stokes substrate instances, does not classify every possible layer-dissolving move, and does not assert that the substrate carrier is unique.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P028-C0026"><data key="label">Sufficiency Closure: The current quotient Q is sufficient for the declared future family F if and only if every declared future probe f∈ F descends through q . Equivalently, for every f:H→ F_f in F there is a map f:Q→ F_f such that f= f q .</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P028-C0027"><data key="label">It also does not assert sufficiency for undeclared probes, which lie outside the current audit scope.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
