    <node id="P028-C0033"><data key="label">Descent-Repair Normal Form: Let q:X→ Q be a quotient map, let F:X→ Y be a map, and let r:Y→ R be a target readout. Then r F descends through q if and only if Delta(q,F,r)=∅ . If the obstruction is nonempty, the canonical repairs are: source refinement, which…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
