    <node id="P032-C0047"><data key="label">Potential construction on a rooted tree: Let G=(V,E) be a finite tree with root r , and let a: E→R be antisymmetric. Define phi(r)=0 and, for v≠ r , phi(v)=phi(par(v))+a(par(v),v). Then a(u,v)=phi(v)-phi(u) for every oriented edge (u,v)∈ E .</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P032-C0048"><data key="label">Finite strictly increasing chains are bounded: If S is a finite set, then every strictly increasing chain of distinct elements of S has length at most |S| .</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0001"><data key="label">Many mathematical frameworks come with audit data alongside their main objects: source ledgers, route registries, residual budgets, status annotations, nonclaim boundaries, and meta-audit records. Audited Operational Realisability (AOR) is the meta-theory of…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0002"><data key="label">full predicate-level non-membership proofs at every level remain framework future work.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0003"><data key="label">Two scope disclosures apply.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0004"><data key="label">The category PreSB_ S consists of typed carriers equipped with declared audit data over S — observation, stage, constraint, rewrite, holonomy, residual, status, nonclaim, and meta-audit registries — together with morphisms preserving the scoped package.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0005"><data key="label">It has eight named strata: observation, stage, constraint, rewrite, holonomy, residual, nonclaim, and meta-audit.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0006"><data key="label">Finally, states the status, scope, and nonclaim boundary, and summarizes the audit-closure meta-theory.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0007"><data key="label">it is accompanied by records of which probes are native, which routes are legal, which residuals remain unpaid, which statements are explicitly outside scope, and which bookkeeping obligations have been accepted.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0008"><data key="label">it abstracts the surrounding bookkeeping question: once a residual, route, status, or nonclaim has been declared, what does it mean for the whole carrier to be audit-closed?</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0009"><data key="label">and the source, interface, observation, stage, constraint, rewrite, holonomy, residual, status, nonclaim, and meta-audit registries form the record layer to which the closure-completion construction will be applied.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0010"><data key="label">PreSB carrier: A PreSB carrier is a tuple C = (H, q, Q, Gamma, R, C-reg, Src, Ifc, Obs, Stage, Constr, Rewrite, Hol, Res, Stat, NC, Meta; S), of seventeen typed fields: legal-quotient carrier and audit data (H,q,Q) ; route registry Gamma ; record registry R a…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0011"><data key="label">Scope record: A scope record S is a typed declaration of the admissible carrier-class, the admissible source ledger, the admissible interface family, and the admissible route registry against which a PreSB carrier is audited. Scope is a first-class field of a…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0012"><data key="label">PreSB morphism: A PreSB morphism f: C→ C&#x27; between two PreSB carriers of identical scope is a tuple of typed scope-preserving field morphisms that commute with the carrier quotient maps, the route registry transports, and the audit form pairings. Morphisms com…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0013"><data key="label">AOR subcategory: The AOR subcategory AOR_ S is the full subcategory of PreSB_ S whose objects are the PreSB carriers C for which the eight-stratum structural defect Xi_ SB ( C) ( ) is zero. Equivalently, every declared record of C is typed, every cited route…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0014"><data key="label">AOR is a full subcategory: The inclusion :AOR_ S PreSB_ S is a fully faithful functor. The defect predicate Xi_ SB ( C)=0 is preserved by isomorphism and reflected by it, so AOR membership depends only on the isomorphism class of the carrier within scope S .</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0015"><data key="label">The isomorphism-invariance statement follows because each audit obligation is a typed field-level condition: transporting a record, route, residual status, nonclaim entry, or meta-audit discharge across an isomorphism changes its presentation, not its existen…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0016"><data key="label">Closure-completion operator: The closure-completion operator Cl_ SB :PreSB_ S →AOR_ S assigns to a PreSB carrier C the carrier obtained as the least fixed point of the monotone-saturation map C C \ minimal AOR-extending operations on C\ on the complete lattic…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0017"><data key="label">The saturation endomap is therefore monotone: adding data before applying the rule cannot remove any typed route, residual status, nonclaim entry, or meta-audit discharge after applying it.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0018"><data key="label">Construction theorem for Cl_ SB: The lattice of AOR-extending operations over a fixed scope S is a complete lattice, and the saturation map of is monotone with respect to the subcarrier order. By the Knaster–Tarski fixed-point theorem the least fixed point ex…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0019"><data key="label">The fieldwise meet of any family keeps precisely the data common to all packages, and the fieldwise generated join adjoins the union of all carrier, route, residual, nonclaim, and meta-audit data while retaining only well-typed scope-compatible entries.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0020"><data key="label">Equivalently, every typed-record, route, residual-status, nonclaim, and meta-audit obligation demanded by the package has already been supplied.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0021"><data key="label">Initiality of saturation steps: Let C be a PreSB carrier of scope S , and let D be an AOR carrier of the same scope. For every PreSB morphism g: C→ D and every minimal AOR-extending operation sigma added by the saturation map S to a candidate package X C , th…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0022"><data key="label">The minimal operation sigma adds exactly one of the audit-completion data types used by the saturation map: typed-record data, route audits, residual statuses, nonclaim entries, or meta-audit discharge records.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0023"><data key="label">Universal property of Cl_ SB: For every PreSB carrier C , every AOR carrier D of the same scope, and every PreSB-morphism g: C→ D , there exists a unique AOR-morphism g:Cl_ SB ( C)→ D satisfying g = ( g) _ C .</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0024"><data key="label">Cl_ SB adjunction: The closure-completion operator Cl_ SB extends to a functor PreSB_ S →AOR_ S which is left adjoint to the inclusion , with unit as in . The counit is the identity on AOR carriers: Cl_ SB =id_ AOR_ S .</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0025"><data key="label">Structural defect and its eight strata: The first diagnostic layer is the structural defect Xi_ SB : the aggregate record of ways in which a scoped PreSB carrier has not yet closed as an AOR carrier. Splitting the defect into strata keeps the failure mode vis…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0026"><data key="label">A missing observation typing, an undeclared stage law, an unwitnessed constraint, an unannotated rewrite, a missing holonomy transport, an unstatused residual, an unregistered nonclaim, and an undischarged meta-audit obligation are different audit failures, e…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0027"><data key="label">Structural defect Xi_ SB: The structural defect Xi_ SB ( C) of a PreSB carrier C is the disjoint sum of its eight defect strata, Xi_ SB ( C) = Sigma_ obs ( C) Sigma_ stage ( C) Sigma_ constraint ( C) Sigma_ rewrite ( C) Sigma_ holonomy ( C) Sigma_ residual (…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0028"><data key="label">Sigma_ obs stratum: The observation defect stratum Sigma_ obs ( C) is the multiset of typed observation records on C whose target codomain, role, source provenance, or evaluation context is not fully declared. The stratum is empty iff every declared observati…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0029"><data key="label">Sigma_ stage stratum: The stage defect stratum Sigma_ stage ( C) is the multiset of stage / refinement entries whose stage law, refinement axis, or compatibility with the route registry is not declared. The stratum is empty iff every entry of Stage has a decl…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0030"><data key="label">Sigma_ constraint stratum: The constraint defect stratum Sigma_ constraint ( C) is the multiset of constraint and budget entries that fail positivity, fail the audit-pairing typing, or are paired with no declared admissible solution. The stratum is empty iff…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0031"><data key="label">Sigma_ rewrite stratum: The rewrite defect stratum Sigma_ rewrite ( C) is the multiset of rewrite records whose source and target presentations, admissibility tags, or blocked-rewrite annotations are not declared. The stratum is empty iff every Rewrite entry…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0032"><data key="label">Sigma_ holonomy stratum: The holonomy defect stratum Sigma_ holonomy ( C) is the multiset of route-dependent memory records whose carrier transport, source-ledger attribution, or nonclaim flag is not declared. The stratum is empty iff every Hol entry has a ty…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0033"><data key="label">Sigma_ residual stratum: The residual defect stratum Sigma_ residual ( C) is the multiset of Schur-typed residuals on C , further decomposed by the thirteen residual types of . The stratum is empty iff every residual record carries a discharge status from the…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0034"><data key="label">Sigma_ nonclaim stratum: The nonclaim defect stratum Sigma_ nonclaim ( C) is the multiset of statements that the carrier needs to exclude (scope boundaries, blocked routes, blocked rewrites, deprecated claims) but that are not registered in NC . The stratum i…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0035"><data key="label">Sigma_ meta stratum: The meta defect stratum Sigma_ meta ( C) is the multiset of meta-audit obligations (provenance trail, version pin, audit pass log, dispute resolution) that are not discharged in Meta . The stratum is empty iff every meta obligation has a…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0036"><data key="label">Eight-stratum decomposition: For every PreSB carrier C , the structural defect Xi_ SB ( C) decomposes as a disjoint sum of the eight strata Sigma_ obs ,\ Sigma_ stage ,\ Sigma_ constraint ,\ Sigma_ rewrite ,\ Sigma_ holonomy ,\ Sigma_ residual ,\ Sigma_ noncl…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0037"><data key="label">The field that creates it also determines its stratum: an observation record belongs to Sigma_ obs , a stage entry to Sigma_ stage , a constraint or budget entry to Sigma_ constraint , a rewrite record to Sigma_ rewrite , a holonomy or route memory record to…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0038"><data key="label">The thirteen-type Sigma_ residual atlas The thirteen-type Sigma-residual atlas: The residual stratum Sigma_ residual tracks unpaid mathematical content rather than missing record syntax. It is refined here along three axes: primary type, atom refinement, and…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
