    <node id="P006-C0040"><data key="label">Residual partial order: The relation _ res on Sigma_ residual is generated by: (i) atom refinement, a _ res b when a is obtained from b by splitting along a finer probe family or stage; (ii) type inclusion, a _ res b when a has b &#x27;s primary type together with…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0041"><data key="label">Residual atom: A residual record a∈Sigma_ residual is an atom if it is minimal under _ res among non-empty records. Equivalently, a has a unique primary type and no proper non-empty refinement.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0042"><data key="label">Atom decomposition: Every residual record r∈Sigma_ residual admits a finite decomposition r= _ i a_i as a disjoint sum of atoms. The decomposition is unique up to permutation, and is computable from the carrier field data.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0043"><data key="label">Residual product: The product of two PreSB carriers C_1 and C_2 over the same scope (componentwise product of all seventeen fields) has residual stratum Sigma_ residual ( C_1× C_2) = Sigma_ residual ( C_1) Sigma_ residual ( C_2) Sigma_ residual ^ cross ( C_1,…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0044"><data key="label">Forced-residual theorem: For each primary residual type Delta_* , there is a fixed minimal set of forced secondary types that any non-empty record of primary type Delta_* must also exhibit. The complete forced-secondary list is recorded in . Forcing is faithf…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0045"><data key="label">AOR-8 statuses and discharge: The atlas classifies residuals by primary type. Discharge requires a second coordinate: a status saying how the atom is paid, blocked, cited, bounded, or deferred to an asymptotic regime. In the base finite-stage theory this is t…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0046"><data key="label">AOR-8 status catalogue: The AOR-8 status catalogue is the eleven-entry vocabulary of discharge statuses for Sigma_ residual records: zero, budgeted, bridged, hidden, moduli, selected, probabilistic, out_of_scope, nonclaim, blocked, approved_other. The asympto…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0047"><data key="label">It separates genuinely closed residuals from budgeted, bridged, selected, probabilistic, out-of-scope, nonclaim, blocked, and externally approved records, so that the cascade layer can compute downstream obligations from the pair consisting of a residual type…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0048"><data key="label">Discharge record: A discharge record on a residual atom a∈Sigma_ residual is a triple (a,s,pi) with s an AOR-8 status (or asymptotic extension) and pi a typed witness payload appropriate to s : a positivity proof for zero; a finite budget bound for budgeted;…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0049"><data key="label">Discharge witness: A discharge witness for a residual record r= _i a_i is a family (a_i,s_i,pi_i) of discharge records, one per atom in the decomposition of r . The witness closes r if every status s_i is a declared base AOR-8 status, or an asymptotic extensi…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
