    <node id="P006-C0051"><data key="label">Cost record: For each pair (t,s) with t a residual type and s a status, the cost record Cost(t,s) is a finite multiset of (t&#x27;,s&#x27;) pairs called the downstream obligations generated by paying a t -atom with status s . Cost records are tabulated in the 143 -entr…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0052"><data key="label">Downstream operator: The downstream operator Down acts on a residual record r with discharge witness (a_i,s_i,pi_i) by Down(r,\ (a_i,s_i,pi_i)\ ) = _i Cost(type(a_i),s_i) viewed as a new residual record of fresh atoms to be statused.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0053"><data key="label">Cost table: The cost table is the function Cost:Types×Statuses→ P_ fin (Types×Statuses) with 13 residual types and 11 base AOR-8 statuses, totalling 143 entries. Cost-free pairs (t,s) are exactly those with Cost(t,s)=∅ .</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
