    <node id="P006-C0055"><data key="label">It also covers the status-family representative rows for any non-explicit type at budgeted, bridged, moduli, selected, probabilistic, out_of_scope, nonclaim, blocked, and hidden.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0056"><data key="label">Cascade graph: The cascade graph of a residual record r is the bipartite labelled multigraph G(r) whose vertices are residual-record atoms and discharge witnesses (alternating layers), and whose edges record the downstream obligations produced by Down . Edges…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0057"><data key="label">Bipartite cascade graph: For every residual record r and every choice of discharge witness, the cascade graph G(r) is bipartite: edges alternate between atom-vertices and witness-vertices, and no edge connects two vertices of the same kind.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P006-C0058"><data key="label">Cascade termination: The cascade graph G(r) is well-founded under the status-multiset measure induced by the AOR-8 status rank and the Dershowitz–Manna multiset extension. In particular every cascade terminates in finitely many discharge steps.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
