    <node id="P053-C0001"><data key="label">The Zermelo–Fraenkel axioms are usually presented as a flat list, adopted because they work. We show that the list factors, theorem by theorem, through a single staged construction discipline—packaging under a membership lens, audited by rank. We then read, a…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P053-C0002"><data key="label">We make no consistency claims, claim no new independence results, and treat every infinitary commitment as a named, priced hypothesis.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P053-C0003"><data key="label">Results: We carry this out concretely, over the hereditarily finite sets HF , where everything is finite and checkable, and then lift the picture to the infinite by an explicit set of commitments.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P053-C0004"><data key="label">The first purchase (S ).: We prove that no finitely generated completion rule, iterated from any hereditarily finite seed, contains an inductive object (Theorem ). Infinity is therefore not a stronger way of iterating; it is a package change. This is the satu…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
