    <node id="P040-C0212"><data key="label">Failed descent becomes useful content: In this case the promoted output is not always a positive solution. When [a]=0 , the audit certifies successful descent and allows a potential. When [a]≠0 , the audit certifies failure of descent. Both outcomes are usefu…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P040-C0213"><data key="label">Forests have no first obstruction: If Gamma is a finite tree, then H^1(Gamma;k)=0. More generally, for a finite forest, H^1 vanishes componentwise. Hence every edge assignment on a tree descends to a global potential, up to the additive constant freedom on ve…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
