    <node id="P058-C0001"><data key="label">What makes a mathematical object useful when it does not live in the layer where the problem is posed? Imaginary numbers are not real, infinitesimals are not real scalars, roots of irreducible polynomials need not lie in the base field, and cohomology classes…</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
