    <node id="P048-C0011"><data key="label">Joinability: Two states b,c ∈ X are joinable if there exists some d ∈ X such that b →^* d and c →^* d.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P048-C0012"><data key="label">Normal forms: A state n ∈ X is a normal form if there is no state m ∈ X such that n → m .</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P048-C0013"><data key="label">Local confluence: The rewriting system (X,→) is locally confluent if for all a,b,c ∈ X , a → b and a → c implies b and c are joinable.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P048-C0014"><data key="label">Elementary peaks and elementary flatness: An elementary peak is a triple (a,b,c) such that a → b, a → c, b ≠ c. The rewriting system (X,→) is elementarily flat if every elementary peak is joinable.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P048-C0015"><data key="label">Reflexive joinability: Every state is joinable with itself.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
    <node id="P048-C0016"><data key="label">Elementary flatness iff local confluence: A rewriting system is elementarily flat if and only if it is locally confluent.</data><data key="ntype">CLAIM</data></node>
