    <node id="WISH:ARC-H1"><data key="label">Define how a theory&#x27;s accessible domain is fixed at formation and the minimum lawful founding data.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H2"><data key="label">Give a complete typed classification of admission mechanisms into a theory domain.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H3"><data key="label">Decide from a rule set or closure operator when no admissible first extension can occur without external provision.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H4"><data key="label">Prove an anti-smuggling law for access growth, adjacent to but stronger than No-Free-Distinction.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H5"><data key="label">Separate co-sourcing from shared access and from independent joining.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H6"><data key="label">Define preregistered, timestamped, priced prospective commitments that can lawfully admit later evidence.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H7"><data key="label">Specify lawful domain growth, expiry, revocation, retraction, and rollback.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H8"><data key="label">Relate founding-domain width to later reachability without equating wider with better.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H9"><data key="label">State the minimum certified preconditions before a pair may enter the join calculus.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H10"><data key="label">Classify mutually independent reasons a lawful join may fail.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H11"><data key="label">Certify that a strict join carries content not available from either parent or a mere product/common refinement.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H12"><data key="label">Require each parent record used in a join to be native or honestly bridged, with no fallback laundering.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H13"><data key="label">Price retention of both parents and the genuinely joint contribution, including possible economies or cross-costs.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H14"><data key="label">Attribute a closure rewrite to theorist, carrier, other theory, observer, environment, or mixed trigger.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H15"><data key="label">State necessary and sufficient conditions for a system to carry and execute its own enabling operation.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H16"><data key="label">Reconcile and sharpen existing layer-birth classes before introducing a new classification.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H17"><data key="label">Give a typed transmission table for upward, downward, and peer interfaces.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H18"><data key="label">Classify loss, ambiguity, and nonfactorization when a parent projects to a child interface.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H19"><data key="label">Determine when certified content from one theory can lawfully become available to a peer without a join.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H20"><data key="label">Define the middle ground between mutual irrelevance and formation of a joint theory.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H21"><data key="label">Make certified mutual irrelevance or obstruction a positive scientific result.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H22"><data key="label">Give prospective commitment a certified temporal order and distinguish preregistration from retrospective fit.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H23"><data key="label">Define and measure route residue around cycles of theories.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H24"><data key="label">State when distinct lawful admission routes produce the same domain state and when order matters.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H25"><data key="label">Test whether evidence-arrival or bracketing order changes a join certificate.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-NG1"><data key="label">No admissible first extension under a closed self-referential admission regime without an allowed seed/bridge.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-NG2"><data key="label">Resemblance-only admission cannot certify an independent strict join and may saturate domains.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-NG3"><data key="label">A prediction cannot be discharged solely by an observation whose admission was defined retrospectively by that prediction.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-NG4"><data key="label">Results proved under total lenses do not transfer automatically to partial, self-owned access domains.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H26"><data key="label">Relate enlargement of access/probe families to dissolution and endogenous manufacture of needles.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H27"><data key="label">Treat prospective commitments as finite, budgeted probes rather than cost-free universal reservations.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-H28"><data key="label">Define residuals left by inaccessible, unadmitted, expired, or failed access claims.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-S1"><data key="label">Require an applicability/bridge certificate for every named law imported from another paper or layer.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-S2"><data key="label">Require evidence that a sound mechanism can actually be reached or fired in the declared substrate.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-S3"><data key="label">Define a privilege as an instrument-accessed particular the system cannot revise from within its declared operations.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-S4"><data key="label">State exactly what one negative, exhaustive negative, and closed-family negative can falsify.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-S5"><data key="label">Judge implementations against normative specifications, not examples that may be incomplete or inconsistent.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-S6"><data key="label">Separate lawfulness, non-vacuity, reachability, actual firing, and occurrence.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-LAB"><data key="label">Build a finite Two-Theory World containing bootstrap, prospective commitment, genuine/obstructed joins, order effects, and nulls.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:ARC-NONGOALS"><data key="label">Preserve the wish list&#x27;s exclusions: do not redo I–VI, universalize partial results, or derive empirical phenomena.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-O1"><data key="label">Define determination, exposure, and recoverability as separate interface coordinates.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-O2"><data key="label">Define a join relative to an admissibility regime, with compatibility, existence, and cost.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-O3"><data key="label">Define enablement as distinct from descent, containment, and fixed-layer causation.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-O4"><data key="label">Record top-down refinement versus bottom-up assembly and test whether they reach the same fixed point.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-A1"><data key="label">Give necessary and sufficient join-existence conditions with free/constrained/no-join cases.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-A2"><data key="label">Prove or refute reduction of the join to a categorical product/pullback under explicit hypotheses.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-A3"><data key="label">Identify join currency, cross-costs, and possible refunds/economies.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-A4"><data key="label">Determine when a join of strict extensions is strict over one or both parents.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-A5"><data key="label">Analyze associativity and bracketing dependence of joins as interaction holonomy.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-B1"><data key="label">Characterize confluence of source refinement and target coarsening at whole-construction scale.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-B2"><data key="label">Find invariants detecting layers reachable only by one construction direction.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-B3"><data key="label">State when a closure fixed point is independent of the initial partition and when it is not.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-C1"><data key="label">Exhibit enablement without factorization or descent.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-C2"><data key="label">Lift the laboratory enablement-time assay to a scoped layer-agnostic law with no-birth control.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-C3"><data key="label">Show that an enabler can be necessary while remaining insufficient to determine the enabled layer.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-C4"><data key="label">Determine composition conditions and accumulated budget, residual, or holonomy along enablement chains.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-D1"><data key="label">Test whether equal determination with different exposure is behaviorally inert exactly when recoverable from auxiliary structure.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-D2"><data key="label">Define exposure overread when a declared distinction is manufactured by an operation the substrate does not perform.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-D3"><data key="label">Determine when a well-formed combination of lawful operations is itself a lawful substrate operation.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-D4"><data key="label">Classify packages with no nontrivial admissible coarse-graining and distinguish genuine rigidity from overconstraint or wrong interface.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-E1"><data key="label">No audited join without a nontrivial payment beyond mere co-presentation.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-E2"><data key="label">A join cannot create distinctions absent from parents plus declared bridge.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-E3"><data key="label">Construct lawful theories with no admissible common joint package.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-E4"><data key="label">Use order-dependent composition to test absence of a global theory potential.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-F"><data key="label">Either develop generators/relations for primitive operations or explicitly defer until categorical apparatus exists.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:CLD-DISC"><data key="label">Use explicit claim grades, countermodel atlas, solved calibrations, nonclaims, mechanization ledger, and no silent universality.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-STATUS"><data key="label">Define a four-stage status ladder: expressible, present/provisioned, reachable by lawful runtime operations, and actually occurrent.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-BOOT"><data key="label">Classify self-bootstrapping capabilities and minimum seed sets for non-self-bootstrapping capabilities.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-SEED"><data key="label">Separate neutral stocking from outcome-rigging using symmetry, task-blindness, preregistration, and carried control coordinates.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-INDEP"><data key="label">Separate ancestry/source independence from behavioral nonfactorization; require join claims to name which one they establish.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-LOCAL"><data key="label">Require destination ownership and contact-before-connection for local interface growth, with countermodels when dropped.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-HORIZON"><data key="label">Specify what finite-horizon non-occurrence implies about reachability and capability.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-OBSERVER"><data key="label">Account for instrument consumption of bounded shared resources before claiming native formation.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-JOINNF"><data key="label">Require parent tuple, ancestry evidence, licensing control, obstruction semantics, and explicit failure meaning.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-NG1"><data key="label">A join mechanism cannot create the first capability needed to execute itself without an admitted seed.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-NG2"><data key="label">Shared ancestry blocks independence-sensitive join claims regardless of behavioral novelty.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-NG3"><data key="label">An observer using bounded shared capacity cannot certify native formation while omitting its occupancy.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-NG4"><data key="label">One negative point cannot refute an existential capability claim; exhaustive closed-family negatives have different force.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-OP1"><data key="label">Name the shadow price of confluence and whether it is dual to a resource constraint.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-OP2"><data key="label">Test whether A-then-B versus B-then-A produces a join obstruction.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-OP3"><data key="label">Determine whether rendezvous is minimal or one of several irreducible physical join primitives.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-OP4"><data key="label">Determine whether join birth can create participants and how it relates to layer birth.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-BRIDGE"><data key="label">Turn lawful cross-paper transport into a reflexive rule governing VII&#x27;s own citations.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-WITHDRAW"><data key="label">Maintain an append-only semantic withdrawal register, including paraphrase sweeps.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MM-NONGOAL"><data key="label">Keep reachability/occurrence, interaction/correspondence, observer/world, and reachability/derivation separations explicit.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-D1"><data key="label">Define a typed interaction record with theory packages, contact surface, and witnessed contact.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-D2"><data key="label">Distinguish coincidence, common refinement, strict join, obstructed join, and fake join.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-D3"><data key="label">Classify rendezvous, sequential transport, shared carrier, mediation, and shared-budget contact.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-D4"><data key="label">Type upward and downward transmission rather than using rhetorical arrows.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-D5"><data key="label">Attach host, instrument, source, audit, and nonclaim records to every interaction claim.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-T1"><data key="label">Construct two theories whose witnessed interaction carries content absent from parents and common refinement.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-T2"><data key="label">Show whether refining a parent can destroy an admissible join.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-T3"><data key="label">Classify vocabulary, budget, record-closure, gluing, and temporal obstructions, with completeness only if proved.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-T4"><data key="label">Separate sequential composition of interactions from interaction of composite theories.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-T5"><data key="label">Identify conserved quantities or contact degrees across joining, if any.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-T6"><data key="label">Determine what laws/records descend through a join and what is necessarily lost.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-T7"><data key="label">Test whether join failure is generically non-attributable to either parent.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-NG1"><data key="label">Relabeling, coarsening, or presentation change cannot manufacture joint predictive content.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-NG2"><data key="label">Common-source re-expression cannot establish an independence-sensitive strict join without an additional independence witness.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-NG3"><data key="label">A higher layer may select/constrain/reinterpret lower possibilities but cannot create lower facts absent from the lower carrier.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-NG4"><data key="label">Budgeted layers cannot have evidenced contact at zero total cost unless an explicit zero-cost channel exists.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-NG5"><data key="label">Bound simultaneously live joins in terms of finite carrier/interface resources.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-B1"><data key="label">Distinguish undergoing closure from performing closure and test whether birth occurs at contact surfaces.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-B2"><data key="label">State finite expressivity requirements for a new layer to be reachable, including ability to alter interaction structure where needed.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-B3"><data key="label">Explicitly separate observer-certified extension from endogenous enablement.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-UP"><data key="label">Test an asymmetry: obstructions/invariants rise by necessity while downward influence selects among already afforded options.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-CIRC"><data key="label">Formulate consistency/fixed-point conditions for mutually constraining layers without self-certification.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-H1"><data key="label">Measure non-associativity/order residue of multi-theory interaction.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-H2"><data key="label">Determine whether identical members assembled in different orders yield the same theory.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-H3"><data key="label">Require null-versus-driven controls for every inter-theory holonomy or arrow claim.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-H4"><data key="label">Test irreversibility of joining beyond entropy production internal to either parent.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-H5"><data key="label">Define simultaneous contact for theories with potentially incommensurable internal times.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-N1"><data key="label">Classify obstruction dissolution by ascent, peer join, refinement, or terminality.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-N2"><data key="label">Characterize obstructions removable by a peer join without ascent.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-N3"><data key="label">Test whether joining can manufacture new localized obstructions.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-N4"><data key="label">Determine additive versus cross-term residual accounting across joins.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-I1"><data key="label">Attach detector, null, and falsifier obligations to every interaction law.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-I2"><data key="label">Specify append-only records sufficient to certify a join after the fact.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-I3"><data key="label">Make source independence, visibility, and capacity preconditions first-class detector obligations.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-I4"><data key="label">Require same-source, no-contact, scheduling, relabeling, and coincidence nulls.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-I5"><data key="label">Represent contact and joins that have begun but have not completed.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-M1"><data key="label">Require source-object/target-object maps before transporting a named theorem.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-M2"><data key="label">Maintain first-class records of failed bridges and retracted interpretations.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-M3"><data key="label">Format each design requirement separately from its imported rationale.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-S1"><data key="label">Treat source independence as a necessary gate for independence-sensitive joins, not a sufficient causal-independence proof.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-S2"><data key="label">Use asymmetric error costs and conservative defaults for first-positive join claims.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-S3"><data key="label">Label every interaction condition necessary, sufficient, both, or neither.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-S4"><data key="label">Publish substrate expressivity requirements for each interaction type before interpreting nulls.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-S5"><data key="label">Tie negative-result force to search-family closure and quantifiers.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
    <node id="WISH:MED-S6"><data key="label">Validate that safety/independence gates are active and not vacuous.</data><data key="ntype">WISH_ATOM</data></node>
